        "Prepare a short description of the business, the decision maker, primary users and an example of the current workflow. If you already have a website or application, its public address and a description of the problems are enough initially. Do not put passwords, service keys, customer records or confidential documents in an enquiry. Explain timing constraints, available content and connections that need investigation; separate essential launch requirements from later improvements. At handover, check agreed scenarios such as mobile use, invalid input, role permissions and recovery after an error. Discuss training, maintenance, backups and technical access explicitly so their scope is understood rather than inferred from a service name."
